.TH HOLOGRAPHIC-EYE 1 "September 2026" "The Holographic Eye" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
holographic-eye \- open and inspect the native Holographic Eye shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B holographic-eye
.br
.B holographic-eye
.RI " help|version|schema|status|probe " "[--json]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
With no arguments,
.B holographic-eye
opens the graphical Holographic Eye.
The shell reads the bearer token from
.I ~/.hermes/eye_token
and safely adds it to the loopback control-plane URL.
It does not print the token.
.PP
CLI commands write human-readable text to a terminal.
They write one JSON object when stdout is a pipe.
.B --json
forces JSON output.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B help
Show command help.
.TP
.B version
Show the installed shell version.
.B --version
and
.B -V
are aliases.
.TP
.B schema
Show the complete JSON interface contract.
.B --schema
is an alias.
.TP
.B status
Check the loopback health endpoint and token file without changing them.
.TP
.B probe
Alias for
.BR status .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command succeeded.
.TP
.B 2
The gateway or token is unavailable. The output supplies a fix.
.TP
.B 3
The arguments are invalid. The output supplies the correct usage.
.TP
.B 4
The graphical shell failed to start. The output supplies a recovery step.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.hermes/eye_token
Local bearer token. The shell reads this file but never prints its contents.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
holographic-eye
holographic-eye status --json
holographic-eye schema
holographic-eye --version
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hermes (1)
